263	// TestCompareUsesSavedParametersNotRegistry proves the historical side
264	// is explained by the declaration the report archived: a same-id
265	// registry entry is neither consulted nor able to complete the saved
266	// parameters, the enabled version never leaks in, and a saved id the
267	// registry never carried is still a valid explanation on its own.
268	func TestCompareUsesSavedParametersNotRegistry(t *testing.T) {
269		// Damage the registered archA entry while the report's own embedded
270		// copy stays intact: the comparison still shows archA's saved
271		// parameters and borrows nothing from the registry.
