3	// End-to-end regression coverage for the historical side of `compare`
4	// through the real command entry point (see TestMain): the version
5	// declaration embedded in the compared archived report must pass the
6	// same integrity proof a `report` query enforces before any comparison
7	// JSON is printed. A written null used to be explained as the built-in
8	// rules and an incomplete declaration used to compare under zeroed
9	// parameters. On a damaged historical declaration the command exits 1,
10	// prints nothing on stdout, and names the target chain, block, the
11	// readable saved version id and the offending rule or field on stderr —
12	// even for a block with no swaps. Success or failure leaves the
13	// archive untouched.
